# "Bigger cartridges" — a cartridge writing to its own flash.
#
# BEFORE is what the linker left in an unused bank, which is what an erased
# chip holds. AFTER is the byte the RAM-resident routine programmed. If the
# routine were run from ROM instead of RAM this would hang rather than fail,
# because 6502-EMULATOR models the busy window — which is the point of it.

cart 512K
timeout 30s

expect ^FLASH CART SAVE$
expect ^BEFORE \$FF$
expect ^AFTER  \$5A$
